    {
      "id": "dusk_dunn_bridge_told",
      "says": [
        {
          "text": "“Crosses nothing.” He laughs, but not much. “Stream went round two hundred years back — there is the old bed, dry as a road. Bridge is pointed, parapet is sound, and I have carted every load of lime that has gone into this parish for twenty years and not one of them went there.”"
        }
      ],
